  "verbalization": "Licorice glycoside D2 is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which serves as a target for multiple compounds, including 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester and Polyphillin C. These compounds, in turn, direct their targets to DMS-79, suggesting a potential pathway where Licorice glycoside D2 may influence DMS-79 through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence indicates that Licorice glycoside D2 acts as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component in epigenetic regulation. This mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets in the complex, suggesting a broader role in cellular processes that could be modulated by Licorice glycoside D2. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Licorice glycoside D2 to influence DMS-79 through epigenetic mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
